  "id": "Compound::DB00769 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortamate is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of molecular relationships that converge on the steroid hormone receptor Nr3c1. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortamate, which resembles other glucocorticoids like Difluprednate and Loteprednol, binds to a common ancestor in the steroid hormone pathway. This ancestor is part of the broader class of corticosteroids, which are known to interact with Nr3c1, a gene involved in the regulation of glucocorticoid signaling. The shared resemblance between Hydrocortamate and other glucocorticoids, combined with their binding to Nr3c1, indicates a potential mechanism of action where the structural similarity to corticosteroids facilitates interaction with the receptor. The evidence from multiple paths highlights a recurring theme of glucocorticoid-like compounds interacting with Nr3c1, suggesting that the relationship is rooted in the structural and functional properties of corticosteroids. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Hydrocortamate may act through a mechanism similar to other glucocorticoids, thereby influencing Nr3c1 activity.",
